# Roc-native interfaces, without the framework tax

Rocci is a small toolchain for authoring HTML in `.rocci`, writing content in
`.rocdown`, adding server-driven interaction with Datastar, and shipping the
same web interface in a desktop window.

```rocci
import Html

@component Greeting = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, {name}</p>
```

[Build your first component →](/getting-started/quickstart/)

## One model from source to screen

Rocci lowers explicit template regions to ordinary Roc `Html` constructors.
Your Roc values and functions stay Roc. The browser receives semantic HTML,
and interaction stays opt-in.

| Surface | Author with | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Components | `.rocci` | Roc functions returning `Html` |
| Documents | `.rocdown` | Markdown plus explicit Roc or Rocci regions |
| Server interaction | `@on` and Datastar actions | HTML documents or targeted SSE patches |
| Desktop apps | `rocci run` and `rocci bundle` | A local HTTP app inside a native webview |
| Documentation | `rocs build` | Deterministic static HTML |

## Designed around visible boundaries

- **Markdown remains Markdown.** A fenced example is displayed, never executed.
- **Templates remain bounded.** Markup is legal in `@component` bodies, not in arbitrary Roc expressions.
- **The server owns state.** Datastar transports HTML patches instead of introducing a second client application.
- **Static stays static.** Rocs compiles prose in Rust and evaluates its Rocci theme once per build.

> Rocci is experimental. The language and toolchain are usable for exploration,
> examples, and documentation, but some packaging and static-site features are
> still under active development.

## Choose a path

- New to the project? Read [What is Rocci?](/getting-started/overview/).
- Ready to type code? Follow the [five-minute quickstart](/getting-started/quickstart/).
- Building server-driven UI? Start with [server actions and Datastar](/guides/server-actions/).
- Writing technical content? See [Rocdown pages](/guides/rocdown-pages/).
- Looking up exact syntax? Open the [Rocci language reference](/reference/rocci/).
